---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import data from '../data/tools.json';
import { siteEditUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<ContentLayout editUrl={siteEditUrl('src/pages/architecture.astro')} title="How Magpie fits together" description="Skills describe the work. Tools connect that work to your agent, services, and project conventions.">
  <div class="arch-flow" aria-label="Skills request capabilities implemented by tools"><div class="surface-card"><h3>Skills</h3><p>The workflow: what to check, prepare, and bring back for approval.</p></div><div class="surface-card"><h3>Capabilities</h3><p>The interface a skill needs, such as reading an issue or drafting mail.</p></div><div class="surface-card"><h3>Tools</h3><p>The implementation for your tracker, model, or other service.</p></div></div>
  <section id="vendor-neutrality"><h2>Choose your tools without rewriting the workflow</h2><p>Skills ask for a capability rather than a named vendor. Adapters implement the interface for each backend, so your project can change its tools while keeping the workflow.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="/docs/vendor-neutrality">Vendor neutrality </a><a href="/tools">Browse tools </a></div></section>
  <section id="organizations"><h2>Keep your project’s conventions</h2><p>Organization profiles supply shared governance vocabulary and tool defaults. Apache and independent projects have starting profiles; other foundations and teams can provide their own.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="/docs/extending">Extend Magpie </a><a href="https://github.com/apache/magpie/tree/main/organizations" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Organization profiles </a></div></section>
  <section id="model"><h2>Explore the reference</h2><p>The capability and tool definitions below come from the framework. Implementation status and supported vendors are available in the tools directory.</p><div class="link-row"><a href="/docs/labels-and-capabilities">Labels and capabilities </a><a href="/docs/adapters/registry">Adapter registry </a><a href="/docs/skill-sources/authoring-a-source">External skill sources </a></div></section>
  <details id="tool-capabilities"><summary>Capability contracts</summary><table class="reference-table"><tbody>{Object.entries(data.contracts).map(([name,description])=><tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details>
  <details id="skill-capabilities"><summary>Low-level capabilities</summary><table class="reference-table"><tbody>{Object.entries(data.substrates).map(([name,description])=><tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details>
</ContentLayout>
